  "findings": [
    {
      "disposition": "resolved",
      "id": "N20V7-F15",
      "severity": "critical",
      "summary": "User-directed spec decision (N30V7-F07 lineage, not an ordinary code defect): a versioned, named-profile host allowlist for source retrieval, closing the gap N70 live-verified -- SourceRetriever's own SSRF-prevention allowlist had never been populated in production at all (retrieval_hosts defaulted to an empty tuple and run_curriculum.py never passed a value), so every retrieval was always denied `host_not_allowlisted` regardless of domain. N20's share of the implementation: (1) egress.py gained `load_retrieval_host_profile(name, path=...)`, returning `(hosts, policy_digest)` for one named profile from policy/retrieval_hosts.v1.yaml -- rejects wildcards, scheme/port/path fragments, non-lowercase, duplicates, and unknown profile names; a curriculum selects a profile by name, never supplies hosts directly. (2) model_nodes.py's m01_discover_unit_sources now rejects every locator (failure_class `candidate_boundary_violation`, routed through repair like any other content-shape violation) whose URL host is not exactly one of the hosts D06 granted in `discovery_authority.allowed_hosts` -- before D06B ever attempts retrieval, and independent of D06B's own identical enforcement at actual fetch time (egress.py, unchanged, already exact-match/HTTPS/DNS-SSRF/allowlisted-redirect-correct once real hosts are wired in -- confirmed by inspection, no code change needed there). (3) The M01 discover prompt now tells the worker the exact allowed_hosts list so WebSearch can be steered toward usable sources, and states plainly that an out-of-list result is never a usable candidate. New regression tests: loader positive/negative (real profile, unknown profile, wildcard, URL-instead-of-host), and M01-discover positive/negative (granted host accepted, non-granted host rejected before retrieval, empty grant denies everything). Two shared full-graph test harness fixtures (test_plan26_adversarial.py, and its N40-owned sibling test_plan26_unit_graph.py) needed `resolved_hosts` added to their authorization declarations so their own scripted M01 candidates -- which the real host-check now also applies to -- keep reaching their intended terminals. Full 8-file N20 suite: 489 passed (up from 482, +7), 1 skipped, 140 subtests passed. Zero scan violations."
    }
  ],
